# Fixture for reactant_count_helper_test: a rate law that reaches the
# reactant_1() placeholder through a helper function (issue #59).  BNG2 2.9.3
# writes the functions as reactant_1, kf, g, _rateLaw1 (= 2*g()).  RM bound
# the rule's reactant count only into the rate law's own evaluation, so g()
# was settled with the placeholder at zero, _rateLaw1 read that zero, and the
# rule never fired.
# Under TotalRate the rate law is the whole propensity, 2*k*A, so each A(s~0)
# flips at rate 2k and Aoff(t) is binomial(100, exp(-2 k t)).
begin model
begin parameters
  k 1e-2
end parameters
begin molecule types
  A(s~0~1)
end molecule types
begin species
  A(s~0) 100
end species
begin observables
  Molecules Aoff A(s~0)
end observables
begin functions
  reactant_1()
  g() = reactant_1()*kf()
  kf() = k
end functions
begin reaction rules
  A(s~0) -> A(s~1)  2*g() TotalRate
end reaction rules
end model
begin actions
  writeXML()
end actions
